# Boot battery guard, drained latch: written when the display reaches
# 0 % (owner decision 2026-10-22, second round: this unit can hard-cut
# before the low-battery shutdown, so that is only a backup). The sim
# boots at 3,450 mV (over the floor) with a clear record
# (IPODUI_SIM_DRAINED=0); 2 s after power-on the cell falls slowly to
# 3,250 mV (IPODUI_SIM_DRAIN_AT_MS, IPODUI_SIM_DRAIN_MV; powermgmt-sim.c).
# The 64 s filter crosses the sim table's 0 % point (3,300) in about a
# minute, still over the sim's disk-safe (3,200): bootbatt_service()
# waits up to 30 s for the disk to be awake anyway, then writes the
# record once (read back as drained). Nothing shuts down.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p16-bootbatt-latch-set.script
# env: IPODUI_SIM_BATT_MV=3450
# env: IPODUI_SIM_DRAINED=0
# env: IPODUI_SIM_DRAIN_AT_MS=2000
# env: IPODUI_SIM_DRAIN_MV=3250
# timeout: 180
# golden: skip
# log: bootbatt latch drained=0 boot mv=3450
# log: bootbatt latch set zero rc=20
# log: bootbatt latch readback=1
# nolog: bootbatt latch set shutdown
# nolog: sys lowbatt empty=1
# nolog: sys deadbatt
# nolog: splash-pass

wait 4000
shot main_menu
wait 120000
shot main_menu_zero
